@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1076 = private unnamed_addr constant [622 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for empty methods in abstract base classes without an abstract\0Adecorator.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AEmpty methods in abstract base classes without an abstract decorator may be\0Abe indicative of a mistake. If the method is meant to be abstract, add an\0A`@abstractmethod` decorator to the method.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom abc import ABC\0A\0A\0Aclass Foo(ABC):\0A    def method(self): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\0A\0A\0Aclass Foo(ABC):\0A    @abstractmethod\0A    def method(self): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `abc`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html)\0A", align 1
