@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1109 = private unnamed_addr constant [565 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary generators that can be rewritten as dict\0Acomprehensions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt is unnecessary to use `dict()` around a generator expression, since\0Athere are equivalent comprehensions for these types. Using a\0Acomprehension is clearer and more idiomatic.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adict((x, f(x)) for x in foo)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A{x: f(x) for x in foo}\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as it may occasionally drop comments\0Awhen rewriting the call. In most cases, though, comments will be preserved.\0A", align 1
