@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1128 = private unnamed_addr constant [2477 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `printf`-style format strings to format logging\0Amessages.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `logging` module provides a mechanism for passing additional values to\0Abe logged using the `extra` keyword argument. This is more consistent, more\0Aefficient, and less error-prone than formatting the string directly.\0A\0AUsing `printf`-style format strings to format a logging message requires\0Athat Python eagerly format the string, even if the logging statement is\0Anever executed (e.g., if the log level is above the level of the logging\0Astatement), whereas using the `extra` keyword argument defers formatting\0Auntil required.\0A\0AAdditionally, the use of `extra` will ensure that the values are made\0Aavailable to all handlers, which can then be configured to log the values\0Ain a consistent manner.\0A\0AAs an alternative to `extra`, passing values as arguments to the logging\0Amethod can also be used to defer string formatting until required.\0A\0A## Known problems\0A\0AThis rule detects uses of the `logging` module via a heuristic.\0ASpecifically, it matches against:\0A\0A- Uses of the `logging` module itself (e.g., `import logging; logging.info(...)`).\0A- Uses of `flask.current_app.logger` (e.g., `from flask import current_app; current_app.logger.info(...)`).\0A- Objects whose name starts with `log` or ends with `logger` or `logging`,\0A  when used in the same file in which they are defined (e.g., `logger = logging.getLogger(); logger.info(...)`).\0A- Imported objects marked as loggers via the [`lint.logger-objects`] setting, which can be\0A  used to enforce these rules against shared logger objects (e.g., `from module import logger; logger.info(...)`,\0A  when [`lint.logger-objects`] is set to `[\22module.logger\22]`).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.basicConfig(format=\22%(message)s\22, level=logging.INFO)\0A\0Auser = \22Maria\22\0A\0Alogging.info(\22%s - Something happened\22 % user)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.basicConfig(format=\22%(user_id)s - %(message)s\22, level=logging.INFO)\0A\0Auser = \22Maria\22\0A\0Alogging.info(\22Something happened\22, extra=dict(user_id=user))\0A```\0A\0AOr:\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.basicConfig(format=\22%(message)s\22, level=logging.INFO)\0A\0Auser = \22Maria\22\0A\0Alogging.info(\22%s - Something happened\22, user)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.logger-objects`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `logging`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/logging.html)\0A- [Python documentation: Optimization](https://docs.python.org/3/howto/logging.html#optimization)\0A", align 1
